      "description": "Watch Tours vs Strasbourg highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 6, 2026. On September 6, 2026, the Ligue 1 clash between Troyes and Strasbourg delivered an unforgettable spectacle filled with tactical shifts and a relentless pursuit of goals. Both sides looked to assert their dominance early in a match that would eventually see the momentum swing dramatically. Early Breakthrough and a Sudden Shift The match ignited early when Troyes took the lead in the 9th minute. Antoine Mille found the back of the net with a clinical left-footed finish following an incisive pass from Anis Ouzenadji . The home side appeared to be in control, but Strasbourg 's resilience began to show as the first half drew to a close. Within a frantic two-minute window, the visitors completely overturned the deficit. Jacobo Ortega leveled the scoring in the 40th minute, and shortly after, Diogo Sousa capitalized on a key pass from Oso to put the visitors ahead before the interval. Strasbourg's Second-Half Dominance The momentum remained firmly with the visitors after the restart. In the 57th minute, Giovanni Reyna extended the lead with a composed finish. As both managers turned to their benches, Strasbourg 's tactical adjustments proved devastating. Samuel Amo-Ameyaw , introduced as a substitute, took center stage by scoring twice in quick succession—first in the 85th minute and again in the 88th following a defensive lapse by Patrick Beach . The scoring spree continued into stoppage time when Conrad Harder added a sixth goal for the visitors. While Jeremy Le Douaron managed to pull one back for Troyes in the 95th minute after an assist from Kandet Diawara , it was a mere consolation. Strasbourg walked away with a deserved 2-6 victory, showcasing a clinical display of finishing that left the hosts with no answers."
